{
  "name": "epanet_pump_flow_control_speed",
  "description": "The same flow-controlled pump network, its reference speed found from EPANET alone (the relative speed at which EPANET's pump passes 18 L/s, by brentq): an independent reference for the solved speed.",
  "source": "WNTR 1.5.0 EpanetSimulator (EPANET 2.2.0); see tests/reference/generate_epanet_cases.py. D-W headloss, GPM INP units, accuracy 1e-5, headerror 1e-9 ft and flowchange 1e-12 gpm (EPANET reads both in the INP units, input1.c:595-596; WNTR writes them unconverted); viscosity VISCOS = 1.1e-5 ft2/s = 1.02193344e-6 m2/s (the project's custom fluid has the same nu; its density, 1000 kg/m3, does not affect the comparison because friction depends only on nu and a surface-pressure head p/(rho g) is converted with the same rho and g on both sides); solver run in 'swamee_jain' mode. Known EPANET biases, all far inside the 0.5% criterion: EPANET's head-loss coefficients use g = 32.2 ft/s2 = 9.81456 m/s2 against our 9.80665 (0.08% in head loss), its minor-loss constant is 0.02517 against the exact 1/(2g(pi/4)^2) = 0.0251730 in US units (0.012%), its GPM flow-unit constant GPMperCFS = 448.831 differs from the exact ft3/(gal/60) by -3.8e-07 (relative, in flow), and its results are float32 (about 1e-7 relative). Pumps: EPANET HEAD curve through the same collinear points (EPANET's piecewise-linear curve then equals our PCHIP), run as stated below. Flow-controlled pump (active): reference speed by scipy.optimize.brentq over the pump's relative speed (EPANET SPEED, h = w^2 H0(q/w)) between its minimum and maximum speeds, xtol 1e-09, for the EPANET pump flow to equal Q_set; expected values from the EPANET run at that speed, rounded to 11 digits as WNTR writes it.",
